    "content": "we have distribution of train data where we want to make samples from the same distribution , for each sample we design a model , normally all the models must have the same performance , for evaluation we use validation set we found that the accuaraccy differs (High variance : when u compute the variance of the smaples and it's high so the accuaraccy will be not consistent ) each model is specify to the training set too much which means is too flexible . we compute the bias : we calculate y - y^  for each model then we take expectation of thee values if it is  high then we have high bias which means we get results less than we expect so will have an underfitting .\nLet's focus on high variance (overfitting) :  We need to reduce the flexibility of the model .\n(complexity , effieciency , effecivness )\nHow we can solve this problem , if we apply random search like searching for any possible solution and we try it but this is unproffesional and it is expensive . We need to give an exact solution or what we call a methadology that by using it we can expalin our porcess :\nAt the begining we hav eto take in consideration is bias ; do we have high bias (we need to consider the performance of the train set ) the solution for it is to make the model more flexible by increasing the number of neurons , layers and iterations then we test again do we still have high bias or do we solve this problem if yes we move on else we repeat the process of adding neurons , layers .... . Now we need to check if we have a high variance to check it we need to use the validation set and we compare it with the performnce of the test set ,if the gap is big we need to reduce the flexiblity using regularization and if it is possible we need to increase the amount of the data ( because a lot of time the data we have doesn't really represent all the possibilties ) .\nRegularization : we use it to reduce the number of possibilities but which possibilties \nComplex model is realted directly to overfitting , we need to analyze the parameter if their value in absolute value is high which means we have overfitting and a complex model .",
