    "id": "note-1792574234620",
    "title": "Lecture Notes",
    "content": "Bias is systematic error that causes unfair outcome .\nDiffrente types of base :\nData bias , algorithmetic bias , social bias , deployement and feedback bias , generative bias .\n<=> Mitigating bias in AI : ( it means that we need to make bias less harmful and less present ) ai bias must be identifieed , assessed , reduced and monitored .\nHow we can mitigate bias : \n**Detecting bias in data :\nCollect diverse and representative data .\nAudit existing data for missing groups , imbalanced representataion and biased labels .\nExamine data quality .\nIdentify groups for which data are insufficient .\nDocument known limitations and potential source of bias .\n**Detecting bias in algorithm :\nConduct regular bias audits .\nTest models using diverse user profiless and real word scenarios .\nCompare relevant performance measures across groups .\nEvaluate intersectional groups where appropriate .\nTest systems under diffrent operating conditions .\n=>Debiasing techniques in AI models :\nReweighting , fair representation learning , synthetic data .\nLimitations : synthetic data can repoduce biases ub the original data or introduce new ones .\nConsideration : No single diabasing techinique works for every model , dataset or application .\n=>Reducing Proxy variables :\nproxy variable is a feature that indirectly represents another characteristc even when that characteristics is not explicitly included .\nMitigation strategies :\nIdentify features that may act as proxies for senstive characteristics.\nExamine their relationships with outcomes and groups disparties .\nAsses whether each feature is necessary justified .\n=>Transperancy and explainable AI :\n**Transparent model developement :\ndocument data sources and collection mothods .\nrecord known data limitations and potential biases .\nexplain model objectives , assumptions and evaluation criteria .\n**Explainable AI :\nexplainable ai mothods aim to make model outputs or behaviours more understandable to relevant .\nTransparenty concerns making relevant information about a system ...\n\n***Ethical and inclusive design : \nEthical Ai frameworks :\nAdopt relevantt ethical principles and translate them into practical requirements such as faireness , accountability , transperancy .\nInclusive design practices :\nEngage diverse communication , particularly historically marginalised groups .\nInclude affected stakeholders during design , testing and deployement .\nExamine how diffrent groups may experience the system .\n\nQ : Name 3 methods that can help detect or mitigate bias in AI systems .\nQ : how should companies n devveloppers take responsibility for biased AI systems .\nQ : Discuss the role of legislations in preventing biased and protecting affected individuals .",
